think big but start small have that big  vision for where you're gonna go with  your business to help keep you motivated  but make sure you're taking steps every  day to move that business forward  otherwise it's all you have is a big  dream sometimes it's so big and so scary  that you don't end up taking any action  to move it forward hi I'm Evan  Carmichael your friend in all things  entrepreneurship and today I'm answering  a question from one of our readers  Jennifer who wants to start a children's  amusement park and is worried that she  only has the option to start big so  thanks for the question Jennifer  congratulations I wanted to start this  business  I'm I'm worried for you it's possible to  start big it's possible to raise a lot  of money and start big but your chances  of success go down dramatically because  you're gonna make a lot of mistakes like  with any business you're gonna make a  lot of mistakes and the more money and  the more you grow the more opportunities  there are for mistakes the best way to  build a business if you can is start  small and build it up and so applying  that to your business how can you do it  you don't have to have a huge amusement  park wrecked in the beginning what I  would do is try to find low-cost ways to  get this thing started I would try to  partner up with local events that are  happening and bring one or two rides out  I would partner up with shopping malls  and use their parking lots on special  days where you can bring some of your  rides out I would try to find cheap ways  to get started it does a couple things  one it helps you test the market do  people want what you're selling it's  great idea to think about it right so  yeah of course everybody wants it but  you never actually know until you start  selling it'll help you see if you  actually like doing this business right  again it can look great on paper but  until you're in it you don't actually  know if you're gonna enjoy this business  or not so  help guide you and they'll start  bringing some money if you can start  bringing in someone and get to the point  where you're at least paying some bills  off at home it's it releases a lot of  stress and a lot of tension allows you  to build a platform for growth so I want  you to have that big vision but find a  lower-cost way to test it out and get  started because I'm afraid that you have  this big dream but nothing is actually  ever gonna happen because it's too big  if you think I have to start big it's  the only way to do it chances are you're  not gonna end up doing anything and  that's my fear for you with my business  my goal is to help a billion  entrepreneurs it's a big number I don't  quite know how exactly that's gonna  happen and we've helped almost 20  million entrepreneurs now through the  website getting to a billion is a big  number that motivates me to keep going  but doesn't paralyze me with fear I'm  still able to do things every day that  grow that business if you look at  companies like harley-davidson and look  at how they got started it was started  by two friends one of them Harley went  in Davidson and they built their first  bike in a shed in their backyard and the  first year they had one bike and the  next year they had three bikes and the  next year they had another three bikes  and the next year they had another seven  bikes and then they started to grow a  little too big for their shed so they  created their own little mini factory  and they kept growing little by little  every year taking those steps and  eventually became one of the most well  known motorcycle companies in the world  they had a big vision but it started  small they took steps and and it doesn't  have to take you years to do it but by  testing it out on a small scale making  partnerships with local businesses  finding ways to get started cheaply and  not spending a lot of money to to test  your concept see if you enjoy doing this  or not and then also start bringing in  some money is in my opinion a much  better way to get started than to try to  act  right from the start my two cents good  luck with the business for those of you  watching if you like the video please  give it a thumbs up below I'd also love  to hear we have to think if you want to  leave a comment under the video thank  you and I'll see you on the next episode  you
 

